------------
INNER ENERGY
------------

The inner energy is: U= E(el) + E(ZPE) + E(vib) + E(rot) + E(trans)
    E(el)   - is the total energy from the electronic structure calculation
              = E(kin-el) + E(nuc-el) + E(el-el) + E(nuc-nuc)
    E(ZPE)  - the the zero temperature vibrational energy from the frequency calculation
    E(vib)  - the the finite temperature correction to E(ZPE) due to population
              of excited vibrational states
    E(rot)  - is the rotational thermal energy
    E(trans)- is the translational thermal energy

Summary of contributions to the inner energy U:
Electronic energy                ...  -2722.58377885 Eh
Zero point energy                ...      1.20378535 Eh     755.39 kcal/mol
Thermal vibrational correction   ...      0.06428508 Eh      40.34 kcal/mol
Thermal rotational correction    ...      0.00141627 Eh       0.89 kcal/mol
Thermal translational correction ...      0.00141627 Eh       0.89 kcal/mol
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Total thermal energy                  -2721.31287587 Eh


Summary of corrections to the electronic energy:
(perhaps to be used in another calculation)
Total thermal correction                  0.06711763 Eh      42.12 kcal/mol
Non-thermal (ZPE) correction              1.20378535 Eh     755.39 kcal/mol
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Total correction                          1.27090298 Eh     797.50 kcal/mol


--------
ENTHALPY
--------

The enthalpy is H = U + kB*T
                kB is Boltzmann's constant
Total thermal energy              ...  -2721.31287587 Eh 
Thermal Enthalpy correction       ...      0.00094421 Eh       0.59 kcal/mol
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Total Enthalpy                    ...  -2721.31193166 Eh


Note: Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds 
      if your molecule has a higher symmetry. Symmetry factor of 1.0 is   
      used for the rotational entropy correction. 
 

Note: Rotational entropy computed according to Herzberg 
Infrared and Raman Spectra, Chapter V,1, Van Nostrand Reinhold, 1945 
Point Group:  C1, Symmetry Number:   1  
Rotational constants in cm-1:     0.003254     0.000317     0.000301 

Vibrational entropy computed according to the QRRHO of S. Grimme
Chem.Eur.J. 2012 18 9955 using a reference frequency of 100.0 cm-1


-------
ENTROPY
-------

The entropy contributions are T*S = T*(S(el)+S(vib)+S(rot)+S(trans))
     S(el)   - electronic entropy
     S(vib)  - vibrational entropy
     S(rot)  - rotational entropy
     S(trans)- translational entropy
The entropies will be listed as multiplied by the temperature to get
units of energy

Electronic entropy                ...      0.00000000 Eh      0.00 kcal/mol
Vibrational entropy               ...      0.11999540 Eh     75.30 kcal/mol
Rotational entropy                ...      0.01984609 Eh     12.45 kcal/mol
Translational entropy             ...      0.02179152 Eh     13.67 kcal/mol
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Final entropy term                ...      0.16163302 Eh    101.43 kcal/mol

